<title>FRANCE: Total in Indonesia production sharing deal.</title>
<headline>Total in Indonesia production sharing deal.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>French energy group Total said on Tuesday that it had signed two production sharing contracts last Thursday with the Indonesian national oil company Pertamina.</p>
<p>&quot;Total will operate both new contract areas and hold a 50 percent interest, together with INPEX, its established partner in production in East Kalimantan in Indonesia,&quot; Total said in a statement.</p>
<p>It said the two new contracts are for the Saliki and Sebawang I blocks off shore of East Kalimantan.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
